      "text": "The clasp had gone stiff with rust. Asha worked it open with a thumbnail. 'Brass,' she said, mostly to herself, 'she always said it was brass, cheap, from the Crawford Market stall, and that's exactly why she never had it insured.' Inside, no photograph -- just a curl of her mother's hair, wound twice around the pin."
